{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Do not call me Naomi; call me Mara.</b> Even though it is written with alef, it follows the pattern of possessors of the hidden heh at the end of alef. <b>Mara</b> instead of heh. And like it: כעגלה דשא (like a calf of the field), according to Rabbi Judah's opinion. And in my view, נועם (no'am) means תענוג (ta'anug, delight), and <b>the bitter</b> is the opposite of delight, and נועם is the food that is sweet."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:23.168131045Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}